#!/bin/sh
# Calling-convention interoperability: callers and callees generated by
# tests/abi/gen_abi.py are compiled by ouro and by clang in all four
# combinations; every mixed build must print exactly what the all-clang
# build prints.
#
# usage: scripts/abi.sh [ouro-binary] [seeds...]
set -u
OURO=${1:-build/ouro}
[ $# -gt 0 ] && shift
SEEDS=${*:-1 2 3 4 5}
TMP=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ouro-abi.XXXXXX")
trap 'rm -rf "$TMP"' EXIT
fail=0
for seed in $SEEDS; do
  python3 tests/abi/gen_abi.py "$TMP" "$seed" 80
  clang -w -c -o "$TMP/callee.clang.o" "$TMP/callee.c" || exit 1
  clang -w -c -o "$TMP/caller.clang.o" "$TMP/caller.c" || exit 1
  for opt in -O0 -O1; do
    "$OURO" -w $opt -c -o "$TMP/callee.ouro.o" "$TMP/callee.c" || exit 1
    "$OURO" -w $opt -c -o "$TMP/caller.ouro.o" "$TMP/caller.c" || exit 1
    clang -o "$TMP/ref" "$TMP/caller.clang.o" "$TMP/callee.clang.o"
    "$TMP/ref" >"$TMP/ref.out"
    for combo in "ouro clang" "clang ouro" "ouro ouro"; do
      set -- $combo
      clang -o "$TMP/t" "$TMP/caller.$1.o" "$TMP/callee.$2.o"
      "$TMP/t" >"$TMP/out" 2>&1
      if cmp -s "$TMP/ref.out" "$TMP/out"; then
        :
      else
        echo "seed $seed $opt: caller=$1 callee=$2 differs from clang+clang"
        diff "$TMP/ref.out" "$TMP/out" | head -6
        fail=$((fail + 1))
      fi
    done
  done
  n=$(grep -c '^f' "$TMP/ref.out")
  echo "seed $seed: $n functions, caller/callee in every ouro/clang combination at -O0 and -O1"
done
[ $fail -eq 0 ] && echo "abi: all combinations match clang" || echo "abi: $fail mismatches"
[ $fail -eq 0 ]
